#section{YAMD language how-to}::

One page per built-in feature. Each page states what the feature is, shows
the source of a working snippet in a code block, and then uses the very same
snippet live — the rendered page demonstrates the behavior it documents.

Render this set as a single page with #code{nix run . -- docs/lang/howto/index.yamd},
or as one page per feature with #code|{nix run . -- docs/lang/howto/index.yamd --mode multi -o out/}|.

All pages share one info table (that is how doc-sets work), so glossaries on
the cross-reference pages list definitions from the whole set.

